    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense for the metadata itself, but what about the content of the records? Some of these maps have these really strange, unidentifiable symbols or hand-drawn figures in the margins that don't correspond to any known topographical features or standard cartographic notation. If I'm describing these \"unidentified entities\" in the 'description' or 'coverage' fields, how do I categorize them without sounding speculative or unscientific?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
