    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the advice. one thing that's bothering me though is the vibe of some of these... there's this one map from the 1840s where the marginalia is very consistent—these small, hunched, mischievous-looking figures are scattered throughout the forested areas, almost like they are part of the landscape. i want to be professional, but it feels weird to just call them 'unidentified figures.' is there any way to use controlled vocabularies or specific taxonomies for 'folklore-adjacent' or 'mythical' motifs so it doesn't look like I'm just making things up or being unprofessional?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
